**Read:** [Measurement uncertainty arising from sampling — Ramsey, Ellison, and Rostron](../sources/Sampling-Uncertainty.lingua#r_3Q0NEPSBDFX8Z1JWAG3C3HRHJM), the complete guide, examples, and corrections; [The Fitness for Purpose of Analytical Methods — Eurachem](../sources/Method-Validation.lingua#r_5XXJY86AVZZ7XRT71EY7TRYDJY), the detection/quantification and sampling sections; [Quantifying Uncertainty in Analytical Measurement — Eurachem/CITAC](../sources/Analytical-Uncertainty.lingua#r_41N1P8BNZH26X9679RHB0THQNS), the near-zero and validation-data discussions.

Extend the measurand back to the sampling target when that is the actual question. A simplified independent decomposition u²_total = u²_sampling + u²_analysis can be useful, but the design and model must justify the components and independence. Preparation, target variation, and shared references can add levels or dependencies. A small analytical uncertainty cannot stand in for the target’s uncertainty.

Use duplicate sampling and independent preparation/analysis to estimate the relevant components, preserving which observations share a sample or preparation. A balanced design and an unbalanced design can support different estimation and cost choices. A lognormal description or uncertainty factor may be more appropriate than an additive symmetric interval for some heterogeneous targets.

Detection and quantification limits concern a method’s performance under definitions, not a universal boundary between an existing and nonexistent substance. An observation reported as below a threshold supplies censored information. Replacing it automatically by zero, half the threshold, or the threshold itself adds an unstated model. Physically nonnegative quantities can also have background-corrected indications on either side of zero.

**Work:** draw a target-to-aliquot hierarchy and specify a duplicate design. Reconstruct one sampling-guide example and identify which variation is estimated at each level. Create a small teaching dataset with several thresholded readings, compare naive substitutions, and state what a censoring-aware observation model would need. Do not claim an exact target mean from the substituted values alone.

For a production delivery, explain how sampling uncertainty, moisture basis, and an acceptance threshold interact. Preserve the definition of the target and the treatment of censored observations in the report so a receiver cannot mistake a laboratory-portion result for a fully characterized shipment.

